  "review": "Each native 7E7390 call uses resource16 (ESP+28 after six pushes), fresh hero result, pinned key, selection0, listenfalse, sound2Dtrue, overFadefalse. Wrapper dispatches through resource pImp slot34, or RET18 on empty; it does not wait. Native task/frame/termination loops follow in caller. Current me:Speak binding is Speak_Blocking and adds its own wait and termination checks. Generated calls therefore remain behaviorally unresolved even when operands and explicit caller loop compile.",
  "requiredLowering": "Use an explicit native resource local for acquisition, speech, task queries and destruction together. LuaRetailResources::Speak provides nonblocking dispatch in reviewed runtime source, but its lifecycle must be generated before changing these calls; do not mix it with cached me:AcquireControl."
